// wdoc section: Websites (the `website` template variant).
page wdoc_websites { sites = [:reference]  title = "Websites"
  h1 "Websites"

  p "The `website` template is a Hugo-style variant of the page template for building marketing and product sites: you bring the *design* (the HTML/CSS — a Figma export, a Claude artifact, a hand-built theme, an externally-built bundle) and slot **wdoc-rendered content** into it. The split is deliberate — HTML/CSS for the fancy shell, wdoc for the words."

  p "Deploy the built-in template with `default_template = :website`, or author your own `template` (recommended for a real design — see below). Scaffold a ready-to-edit project with `wcl init website ./my-site`."

  h2 "Three new pieces"

  p "On top of the ordinary template mechanism (`Sites & Templates`), the `website` workflow adds:"

  list {
    li "**Named slots** — a layout declares `slot hero: content?`; a page fills it with bare `hero { … }`, and the layout places its typed handles with `slot(c, :hero)`. Loose page blocks implicitly fill the reserved `content` slot."
    li "**Head assets** — the `site` block's `stylesheets` / `scripts` / `fonts` fields add `<link>` / `<script>` to every page `<head>`; the `assets` field copies a whole folder (a Vite/webpack `dist/`) into the output verbatim. A layout can also emit head content itself with the `wdoc_head_*` helpers."
    li "**Composable layouts** — combine raw HTML fragments with `Html` elements and typed slot placements, so the shell can still start from an exported or hand-built design."
  }

  h2 "Authoring a layout"

  p "A `template` declares its slots and returns fundamentals. Raw fragments can interpolate `${c.title}`; place declared content structurally with `slot(c, :name)`. A reference to an undeclared slot is a render error."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
template site_main {
  slot content: content
  slot hero: content?
  slot footer: content?
  render = fn(c: TemplateCtx) -> list<Html>
    flatten([
      // Head content the layout owns (the site's `stylesheets` /
      // `scripts` add the rest).
      wdoc_head_meta("viewport", "width=device-width, initial-scale=1"),
      [
        raw($<<HTML
          <header class="nav">
            <a class="brand" href="index.html">${c.title}</a>
            <nav><a href="index.html">Home</a></nav>
          </header>
        HTML
        ),
        el("section", ["hero"], slot(c, :hero)),
        el("main", ["content"], slot(c, :content)),
        el("footer", ["foot"], slot(c, :footer)),
      ],
    ])
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Heredoc terminator" { class = ["note"]
    body = "The closing `HTML` delimiter must sit alone on its line — `HTML ) ],` on one line is an unterminated heredoc. Put the closing bracket on the next line."
  }

  h2 "Authoring content with slots"

  p "A page joined to a `:website` site renders normally; fill any declared named slot with a bare block of the same name. The fill is layout-agnostic; use `name? { … }` when the page may select a layout without that slot."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
page index { sites = [:web]  start = true
  hero {
    h1 "Build something great"
    p "The design lives in CSS; the words live here."
  }

  h2 "About this page"
  p "Everything outside a named fill lands in the reserved content slot."

  footer {
    p "© Built with WCL + wdoc."
  }
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Wiring the design's assets"

  p "Ship the design's stylesheet and script with the site. `assets` copies a folder verbatim into the output (resolved relative to the document); `stylesheets` / `scripts` / `fonts` link files into every page `<head>` (hrefs are emitted verbatim, so they may be a copied asset, a shipped `file`, or a URL):"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
site web {
  default_template = :site_main
  title       = "Acme"
  root        = true
  assets      = ["assets"]                 // copies ./assets/ → _site/assets/
  stylesheets = ["assets/site.css"]        // <link> in every <head>
  scripts     = ["assets/app.js"]          // deferred <script> in every <head>
  fonts       = ["https://fonts.example/Inter.css"]
}
WCL
  }

  p "Because `assets` copies the folder unchanged, the same field takes an externally-built bundle — point it at a Vite or webpack `dist/` and reference the hashed files it emits."

  h2 "Head from the layout"

  p "When slots or site fields aren't enough, a layout (or a part it calls) can emit `<head>` content directly by returning a `Head` fundamental at the **top level** of its list. The `wdoc_head_*` helpers wrap the common cases:"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Helper"                          | "Adds to the page head"                |
      | "`wdoc_head_stylesheet(href)`"    | "`<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href>`"     |
      | "`wdoc_head_script(src)`"         | "deferred `<script src>`"              |
      | "`wdoc_head_font(href)`"          | "a web-font `<link rel=\"stylesheet\">`" |
      | "`wdoc_head_meta(name, content)`" | "`<meta name content>`"                |
      | "`wdoc_head_raw(html)`"           | "verbatim head HTML"                   |
  }

  callout "Top level only" { class = ["note"]
    body = "A `Head` is hoisted only when returned at the layout's top level. A `Head` nested inside the body renders to nothing — it never leaks into `<body>`."
  }

  h2 "The default layout"

  p "`default_template = :website` uses a built-in, theme-aware shell (sticky header with the title + `menu`, optional `banner` and `hero` slots, the content with an optional `sidebar` slot, and a `footer` slot). When the site sets `search = true` / `theme_toggle = true`, the header grows a right-side controls cluster with the search box and the standard light/dark toggle; with neither flag the header is unchanged. It's a fine starting point and a reference to copy: `wdoc_website_layout(c)` is its whole body, composed from `wdoc_part_website_css()`, `website_header(c)`, and slot-aware parts."

  h2 "Scaffold"

  p "`wcl init website ./my-site` generates a complete project: `main.wcl` (the site + head assets), `theme.wcl` (a custom slot-declaring layout), `components.wcl` (starter landing components — hero, feature cards, steps, footer — to edit or replace), `content.wcl` (the page, built from those components + named fills), and `assets/site.css` + `assets/app.js`. Build it with `wcl wdoc build my-site/main.wcl --out my-site/_site`."

  h2 "Site fields"

  type_table { type = SiteConfig }
}
